## Key Design Architecture (Revision 2)

### 1. Database Isolation & Lifecycle Strategy
```mermaid
flowchart LR
    subgraph TestEnvironment [Test Host - Environment: Testing]
        WAF[CustomWebApplicationFactory]
        TestConfig["ConnectionStrings:DefaultConnection\n= Data Source=urlshortener.functionaltests.db"]
        TestDB[("urlshortener.functionaltests.db\n(Created on Init, Deleted on Dispose)")]
    end

    subgraph ProductionEnvironment [Protected Environment]
        ProdDB[("urlshortener.db\n(NEVER TOUCHED)")]
    end

    WAF --> TestConfig
    TestConfig --> TestDB
```

- **Configuration Override:** In `CustomWebApplicationFactory.ConfigureWebHost`:
  - Sets `builder.UseEnvironment("Testing")`.
  - Injects `ConnectionStrings:DefaultConnection = "Data Source=urlshortener.functionaltests.db"` into the host configuration via `ConfigureAppConfiguration`.
- **Database Lifecycle:**
  - `InitializeAsync()`: Ensures `urlshortener.functionaltests.db` is deleted if an orphaned instance exists from a previous run, then executes `EnsureCreatedAsync()`.
  - `DisposeAsync()` / `Dispose()`: Closes all active connections and cleans up `urlshortener.functionaltests.db` and any `-shm`/`-wal` companion files.
- **Safety Assertions:** Tests can assert that the active connection string does NOT contain `urlshortener.db`.

### 2. Asynchronous Analytics Pipeline Verification Strategy
The analytics pipeline is decoupled via `System.Threading.Channels`:
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Test as Functional Test Runner
    participant API as UrlEndpoints (GET /{shortCode})
    participant Channel as ClickEventChannel (Bounded Buffer)
    participant Worker as AnalyticsProcessingWorker (HostedService)
    participant DB as AppDbContext (urlshortener.functionaltests.db)
    participant Analytics as UrlEndpoints (GET /analytics)

    Test->>API: GET /{shortCode} (User-Agent: Runner/1.0, Referer: https://ref.com)
    API->>Channel: TryWrite(clickEvent)
    API-->>Test: 302 Found (Location: https://example.com)
    Note over Test: Redirect received immediately (<10ms)
    
    par Async Worker Loop
        Worker->>Channel: ReadAllAsync() batch
        Worker->>DB: AddRangeAsync(clicks) & SaveChangesAsync()
    end

    loop Polling Helper (every 50ms up to 3s)
        Test->>Analytics: GET /api/v1/urls/{shortCode}/analytics
        Analytics->>DB: Query totalClicks, topReferers, recentClicks
        Analytics-->>Test: 200 OK (ClickAnalyticsResponse)
    end
    Note over Test: Assert totalClicks == 1, UserAgent == "Runner/1.0", Referer == "https://ref.com"
```

- A polling assertion helper `WaitForAnalyticsAsync(string shortCode, Func<ClickAnalyticsResponse, bool> condition, TimeSpan timeout)` queries the analytics endpoint with a short interval (50ms) up to a 3-second ceiling. This tests the real asynchronous pipeline deterministically without arbitrary thread sleep delays.

### 3. Non-Auto-Redirecting HTTP Client
- Testing HTTP 302 requires preventing the `HttpClient` from automatically executing an outbound HTTP GET to the target URL.
- `CustomWebApplicationFactory` exposes:
  ```csharp
  public HttpClient CreateNonRedirectingClient() =>
      CreateClient(new WebApplicationFactoryClientOptions { AllowAutoRedirect = false });
  ```
- All redirect assertions verify:
  - `response.StatusCode == HttpStatusCode.Found` (302).
  - `response.Headers.Location.ToString() == expectedOriginalUrl`.

